# A `.wwcell` is a SPEC, not geometry: one line, pipe-separated.
#
#   <plugin path or name> | <worldspace EDID> | <cellX>,<cellY> | <block size> [| <overlay>]
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF SPEC LINES.
#
# tests/spells/cell_open.sh passes it on the command line while WW_CELL_OPEN
# carries the real spec. Empty is the point: if the environment spec is ever
# silently ignored, the open FAILS and says "empty.wwcell has no spec line",
# instead of quietly drawing whichever cell this file happened to name. A
# fixture that can stand in for the thing under test cannot detect its absence.
#
# For a spec you can actually open by hand, see sanctuary.wwcell beside this.
